   Perspective, Penn State Univ, University Pk, PA, AUG 19-22, 2005},
Abstract = {Mirror neurons are defined as neurons in the monkey cortex which respond
   to goal oriented actions, whether the behavior is self-generated or
   produced by another. Here we briefly review this literature and consider
   evidence from behavioral, neuropsychological, and brain imaging studies
   for a similar mirror neuron system in humans. Furthermore, we review
   functions of this system related to action comprehension and motor
   imagery, as well as evidence for speculations on the system's ties with
   conceptual knowledge and language.},
