Abstract = {Humans produce temporarily stable, genetically mediated odour signatures
   and possess the ability to recognise, discriminate and identify other
   people through the sense of smell. The capability of self, gender, kin
   and non-kin odour recognition plays a role in social interactions. It
   seems that despite the stability of olfactory cues, the hedonic quality
   of body odour may vary over time.},
